 ## Retries
 
-Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
-can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
-drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
+Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends a fresh idempotency key because the gateway sometimes rejects a
+retried capture with a "duplicate idempotency key" error.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The gateway can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024
+retries that drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice. Fresh keys therefore risk duplicate charges
+after a timeout. Follow [Gateway timeouts](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) to investigate timed-out captures; this
+does not prevent duplicate charges.
 
